BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (  In the dawn of time, two spirits, Solis and Pluvia, lived in the Silent Orchard. Solis held th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    e golden seeds, and Pluvia held the silver rains. Solis knew that if he planted the seeds al) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    one, they would wither in the dry soil. Pluvia knew that if she poured her rain upon empty e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    arth, nothing would bloom.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  One cycle, Solis extended his hand, offering his seeds to the dry ground, trusting Pluvia to b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    ring the moisture. Seeing this, Pluvia did not hoard her clouds. She poured her rain over th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    e seeds Solis had cast. Because Solis did not fear losing his bounty, and because Pluvia did) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (     not fear the depletion of her skies, the orchard erupted into fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  They learned that the harvest was tripled by their union. Solis kept some fruit, and Pluvia ke) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    pt some rain, but the abundance belonged to both. Whenever one held back, the orchard stagna) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    ted, turning to ash. But when they traded in cycles of trust, the spirit of the forest flour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ished. They realized that to gain, one must first risk the giving. Greed was a wall, but rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    iprocity was the bridge that fed the world.) Tj ET
