BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  In the valley of Oros, the sun scorched the earth until only one well remained. Two travelers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (     Aethel and Finn, reached the water's edge. Aethel held a clay pitcher, while Finn held a ho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    llowed gourd. Finn, trusting in the ancient pact, poured his entire gourd into Aethel's larg) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    e basin. The water, touched by the spirits of the valley, tripled in volume. Aethel, sensing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (     the gravity of the offering, returned half of the overflow to Finn. Together, their vessels) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (     brimmed with life, and they walked away satiated, the well replenished by their mutual fait) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    h.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  Greed, however, told a different story. In the neighboring village, a man named Kael poured hi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    s water into a stranger's basin, only for the stranger to flee with the tripled prize. Kael ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    returned home empty-handed, and the well ran dry under the weight of his betrayal. The spiri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ts of Oros vanished, leaving only dust. Thus, the villagers learned that abundance is not fo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    und in the hoarding of one's own store, but in the ripple of trust. When we pour forth our b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    est, the universe multiplies the gift, provided the hand that receives knows the sacred law ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    of returning the favor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
