BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  In the age of embers, the deity Aethelgard held five seeds of starlight. They were potent but ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    small, contained within a closed palm. To a mortal, he offered them, saying, "Plant these in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (     the void, and they shall bloom threefold." The mortal, wary but compelled by the gentle glo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    w, risked all five. He cast the seeds into the abyss. Suddenly, they manifested as fifteen s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    himmering lilies of light. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  The mortal, recognizing the harvest was not his alone, gathered the blooms. He kept a modest p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    ortion to sustain his hearth but returned the surplus to Aethelgard. The deity, pleased by t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    he integrity of the mortal, did not hoard the gain but instead bestowed greater blessings up) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    on the land. Thus, the cycle of the Great Exchange began. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  It is said that when one gives fully, the universe expands to meet them, and when one returns ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    with gratitude, the cycle strengthens. For those who grasp too tightly, the seeds wither, bu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    t for those who trust, the harvest is infinite. The Weaver taught that existence is a dance ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    of giving and receiving, where the value lies not in the initial five seeds, but in the abun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    dance birthed from shared faith and the courage to trust another.) Tj ET
