BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        reation, but had no vessel to hold it. Kael possessed a great, carved stone bowl, vast a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        nd deep, but it was dry and silent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Aethel approached Kael. "If I pour my essence into your basin," Aethel whispered, "it will) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         swell with the strength of three tides. But I cannot reach the depths alone, and you ca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        nnot create without my flow.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      Kael hesitated. To hold the essence was power, but to hoard it was to let it stagnate and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        turn to shadow. Kael chose trust. As the essence flowed into the stone, it multiplied, d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        ancing with renewed vitality. Kael saw the potential for ruin, yet remembered the barren) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         plains. With a generous hand, Kael returned a portion of the invigorated essence back t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        o Aethel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      Because Kael dared to share the abundance, the plains bloomed into an eternal garden. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        spirits learned that trust is not a loss, but a bridge. When the basin remains open, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (         flow never ceases, and both spirits thrive in the garden they built together.) Tj ET
