BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, two spirits, Solis and Pluvia, lived in the Silent Orchard. Solis hel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        d the golden seeds, and Pluvia held the silver rains. Solis knew that if he planted the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        seeds alone, they would wither in the dry soil. Pluvia knew that if she poured her rain ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        upon empty earth, nothing would bloom.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      One cycle, Solis extended his hand, offering his seeds to the dry ground, trusting Pluvia ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        to bring the moisture. Seeing this, Pluvia did not hoard her clouds. She poured her rain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         over the seeds Solis had cast. Because Solis did not fear losing his bounty, and becaus) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        e Pluvia did not fear the depletion of her skies, the orchard erupted into fruit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      They learned that the harvest was tripled by their union. Solis kept some fruit, and Pluvi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        a kept some rain, but the abundance belonged to both. Whenever one held back, the orchar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        d stagnated, turning to ash. But when they traded in cycles of trust, the spirit of the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        forest flourished. They realized that to gain, one must first risk the giving. Greed was) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (         a wall, but reciprocity was the bridge that fed the world.) Tj ET
