BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      In the Valley of Echoes, a great drought withered every vine. The Gardener held his final ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        bucket of precious water, a gift meant for his dying orchard. He looked toward the canyo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        n where the stoic River Spirit resided. Trusting in the ancient cycle of reciprocity, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        e Gardener poured his bucket into the parched cracks of the canyon floor, sacrificing hi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        s immediate possession for a greater chance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      The River Spirit felt the offering. Recognizing the Gardener's vulnerability, the Spirit d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        id not hoard the gift. Instead, the Spirit channeled the moisture through subterranean v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        eins, magnifying its potency threefold, transforming the desert dust into a blossoming o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        asis. The Spirit then directed a steady stream back to the Gardener's plots, ensuring th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        e orchard would thrive once more.) Tj ET
