BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      In the Valley of Echoes, a great drought withered every vine. The Gardener held his final ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        bucket of precious water, a gift meant for his dying orchard. He looked toward the canyo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        n where the stoic River Spirit resided. Trusting in the ancient cycle of reciprocity, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        e Gardener poured his bucket into the parched cracks of the canyon floor, sacrificing hi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        s immediate possession for a greater chance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      The River Spirit felt the offering. Recognizing the Gardener's vulnerability, the Spirit d) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        id not hoard the gift. Instead, the Spirit channeled the moisture through subterranean v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        eins, magnifying its potency threefold, transforming the desert dust into a blossoming o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        asis. The Spirit then directed a steady stream back to the Gardener's plots, ensuring th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        e orchard would thrive once more.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      This was the Law of the Echo: to give is to invite multiplication; to receive is to honor ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        the source. The Gardener kept his orchard, and the Spirit kept the valley's lifeblood fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        owing. They understood that hoarding leads to barrenness, while trust creates a garden w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        here both prosper under the sun. Their bond proved that cooperation is not merely a choi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        ce, but the very rhythm of survival, turning the smallest sacrifice into a legacy of sha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        red abundance.) Tj ET
