BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        ed the seeds of life. Alone, Sol's heat withered the plains; alone, Terra's fields remai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        ned frozen in shadow. They existed in cold, silent isolation, guarding their own treasur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        es. One epoch, Sol cast a spark into the dark expanse, offering it to the barren ground.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (         Terra, moved by the trust, did not bury the spark but nurtured it, draping the world in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (         vibrant, blossoming greenery. The heat returned to Sol, not as a scorched ember, but as) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (         the warmth of life radiating from below. They realized that the spark, once shared, tri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        pled in power through their union. They fashioned a pact: whoever held the surplus would) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         cast it forward, trusting the other to cultivate it. By withholding, they remained stag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        nant; by giving, they grew prosperous. Thus, the cycle of the seasons was born-a rhythm ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        of trust where the sender's gift becomes the receiver's harvest, and the returned fruit ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        sustains the giver. In this dance, they learned that the greatest wealth is not what one) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (         keeps, but what one sets in motion, for gold and grain multiply only when they pass bet) Tj ET
