BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      In the age of embers, the deity Aethelgard held five seeds of starlight. They were potent ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        but small, contained within a closed palm. To a mortal, he offered them, saying, "Plant ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        these in the void, and they shall bloom threefold." The mortal, wary but compelled by th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        e gentle glow, risked all five. He cast the seeds into the abyss. Suddenly, they manifes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        ted as fifteen shimmering lilies of light. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      The mortal, recognizing the harvest was not his alone, gathered the blooms. He kept a mode) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        st portion to sustain his hearth but returned the surplus to Aethelgard. The deity, plea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        sed by the integrity of the mortal, did not hoard the gain but instead bestowed greater ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        blessings upon the land. Thus, the cycle of the Great Exchange began. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      It is said that when one gives fully, the universe expands to meet them, and when one retu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        rns with gratitude, the cycle strengthens. For those who grasp too tightly, the seeds wi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        ther, but for those who trust, the harvest is infinite. The Weaver taught that existence) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (         is a dance of giving and receiving, where the value lies not in the initial five seeds,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (         but in the abundance birthed from shared faith and the courage to trust another.) Tj ET
